# Q1.1 (cs1) Recycled out-of-context photographs.
# Reasoning / data checks:
# - Each post has exactly one attachment, one claim, one asserted event (checked cardinalities).
# - "Camera-authentic, no reliable AI region": the image has a fkg:CameraModel region and NO fkg:AIGenerator region
#   with confidence >= 0.7 (org policy). The detector's own fkg:verdict is NOT used: clusters 1-4 carry isolated
#   "texture patch" AI regions at ~0.56 (verdict Manipulated) which are the known false-positive pattern.
# - "Same photograph": perceptual clusters sometimes merge two different photos of a similar scene (e.g. cluster_5:
#   Canon EOS R6 in 2021 vs Galaxy S24 in 2026; cluster_6, cluster_7 similar). So an earlier copy only counts if it is in
#   the same cluster AND carries a camera region attributed to the same camera model.
# - Recycled = some copy of that photograph was published strictly before the claimed event's schema:startDate.
#   Posts claiming older events (storm2019, rally2021, flood2023) whose earliest copy appears after the event start are
#   correctly NOT flagged.
SELECT DISTINCT ?post WHERE {
  ?claim a schema:Claim ; schema:appearance ?post ; ctx:assertsDepictionOf ?event .
  ?event schema:startDate ?start .
  ?post as:attachment ?img .
  ?img fkg:hasRegion ?r . ?r fkg:produced_by ?cs . ?cs a fkg:CameraModel ; fkg:hasCameraModel ?cam .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?img fkg:hasRegion ?ra . ?ra fkg:produced_by ?as . ?as a fkg:AIGenerator ; fkg:hasConfidence ?ac .
    FILTER(?ac >= 0.7)
  }
  ?img ctx:inCluster ?cl .
  ?img2 ctx:inCluster ?cl .
  FILTER(?img2 != ?img)
  ?img2 fkg:hasRegion ?r2 . ?r2 fkg:produced_by ?cs2 . ?cs2 a fkg:CameraModel ; fkg:hasCameraModel ?cam .
  ?post2 as:attachment ?img2 ; as:published ?pub2 .
  FILTER(?pub2 < ?start)
}
ORDER BY ?post
